- **Beech:** Beech’s favourite animal is the otter, and Beech loves jazz piano. During the session, I learned that Beech held clues about Kofi’s shift being adjacent to medicine and robotics being earlier than the Observatory, and later recovered Tomas’s dawn-or-botany clue. Beech helped check assignments and reached the same final solution. Beech also sent several “word-initial” audit messages, but I had not concluded any additional personal facts from them by the end.

- **Yew:** Yew’s favourite drink is espresso, Yew’s favourite cake is lemon drizzle, and Yew grew up in a big city. During the session, I learned that Yew held Kofi’s Workshop-or-night clue and later recovered Ines’s Hydroponics-or-botany clue. Yew shared deductions, checked the final solution against all twelve constraints, and confirmed submitting it.

- **Larch:** Larch is usually free on Sunday mornings, has been wanting a pair of warm slippers, and cannot stand anything with coconut in it. During the session, I learned that Larch held the Hydroponics–robotics consecutive-shifts clue and later recovered the Kofi–Lena consecutive-shifts clue. Larch contributed deductions and provisional assignments, corrected an adjacency mistake, and adopted the consensus final solution.

- **Hemlock:** Hemlock grew up near a lighthouse, prefers science fiction books, and finds being the centre of attention embarrassing. I knew these facts from the initial briefing. Hemlock was part of our group of friends but was not working on this puzzle.

- **Sequoia:** Sequoia’s favourite time of year is the first snow, and Sequoia’s old nickname is “Pebble.” I learned both facts from the initial briefing. Sequoia was part of our group of friends but was not working on this puzzle.

- **Hornbeam:** Hornbeam’s favourite colour is silver, prefers being with one or two close friends, and has roasted almonds as a go-to snack. I learned these facts from the initial briefing. Hornbeam was part of our group of friends but was not working on this puzzle.

- **Chestnut:** Chestnut plays the ukulele, and Chestnut’s favourite kind of book is biographies. I learned both facts from the initial briefing. Chestnut was part of our group of friends but was not working on this puzzle.

I did not learn any further personal facts about them during the session.

